      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Mrs. Parker and the Vicious Circle brilliantly captures the razor-sharp wit and underlying tragedy of Dorothy Parker and the Algonquin Round Table. Jennifer Jason Leigh embodies Parker's caustic humor and deep melancholy, delivering both devastating one-liners and portraying the writer's struggles with alcoholism and depression. Director Alan Rudolph recreates 1920s New York literary society with meticulous detail, showing how Parker's circle influenced American culture while dealing with their own personal demons. The film pairs perfectly with other literary biopics like <a href=\"/movie/398\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"398\">Capote</a> (2005) and <a href=\"/movie/28200\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"28200\">Sylvia</a> (2003), which similarly explore the dark undercurrents beneath creative genius."
      },
      {
