      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's depiction of 1920s Manhattan literary culture connects to a rich tradition of New York intellectual life on screen, from <a href=\"/movie/5143\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"5143\">Hannah and Her Sisters</a> (1986) to <a href=\"/movie/29193\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"29193\">The Spanish Prisoner</a> (1997). Rudolph captures the era's mix of glamour and grit, showing both the sparkle of the Algonquin Hotel and the cramped offices where Parker wrote her reviews."
      }
